00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:36.440
You were half trying.

00:26:36.460 --> 00:26:43.080
I think that the music just underscores the travesty that is the entire game mode because

00:26:43.080 --> 00:26:49.920
I played through figure skating four times and the first three times I got zeros across

00:26:49.920 --> 00:26:52.720
the board. I could not land a single trick.

00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:56.840
Did you land something? Because I could start the move and then I would fall.

00:26:57.020 --> 00:26:58.040
Yeah. And I was like, what do you have to do?

00:26:58.040 --> 00:27:03.800
Then I was reading the manual between every run and then I finally got a 0.7.

00:27:04.220 --> 00:27:06.740
I landed two tricks and I fell twice.

00:27:07.100 --> 00:27:11.480
I landed one trick in all of my attempts and I still got zeros.

00:27:11.820 --> 00:27:14.800
This is what I was talking about where I think there are just, there are too many inputs

00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:15.820
that you need on this.

00:27:15.960 --> 00:27:17.940
Yeah. Let's run through this for a second.

00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:20.940
So to begin skating, press button A.

00:27:21.260 --> 00:27:23.900
To skate forward, press the controller to the right.

00:27:24.240 --> 00:27:27.400
Note, you must be skating forward when your time runs out.

00:27:27.520 --> 00:27:28.460
Otherwise, you'll fall.

00:27:28.640 --> 00:27:36.580
Why? Then to begin a move, hold down the controller in the direction of the move you want to make

00:27:36.580 --> 00:27:39.920
and press and release button A.

00:27:40.360 --> 00:27:43.620
Now the release is important there because then to complete

00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:48.520
the move, you release the controller and press button A again.

00:27:48.880 --> 00:27:54.580
It's a very convoluted control scheme that only makes sense once you've read it like five times.

00:27:54.740 --> 00:27:57.300
The pressing button A again to land is really weird.

00:27:57.300 --> 00:28:01.400
We also have to lift your left thumb up at a certain point.

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:03.900
Yeah. It doesn't say when the timing is.

00:28:03.980 --> 00:28:07.460
You don't know if you're supposed to press A as you're landing or right before you land

00:28:07.460 --> 00:28:09.640
or whatever. I only landed one thing, like I said.

00:28:09.860 --> 00:28:11.100
I don't really know how I did.

00:28:11.100 --> 00:28:12.840
Well, one's better than none and that's me.

00:28:12.840 --> 00:28:14.720
No, I didn't land a single move.

00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:15.840
I don't think I landed any either.

00:28:16.100 --> 00:28:21.060
So don't worry. I mean, score-wise, it wasn't better than none because I still got zeros.

00:28:21.280 --> 00:28:25.340
It is very realistic though because I probably also wouldn't have been able to land any moves.

00:28:25.720 --> 00:28:27.700
So. Yeah. Like in real life.

00:28:28.060 --> 00:28:29.120
Oh, that's true. Yeah.

00:28:29.120 --> 00:28:33.640
Me too. But this is specifically what I meant in my initial impression when I was saying that

00:28:33.640 --> 00:28:36.520
there's just, there's too much to these games.

00:28:36.660 --> 00:28:39.120
Like there's more to it than I expected and it's a little too much.

00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:48.220
And now I just want somebody to imagine that in this game, you, somebody managed to do a

00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:54.640
camel spin into a sit spin and then land it because that's the maximum, that's worth 1.2

00:28:54.640 --> 00:28:57.980
points in figure skating in the game.

00:28:57.980 --> 00:29:04.100
And that means that they jumped into the air, released the A button, had the, had the up

00:29:04.100 --> 00:29:05.060
arrow input held.

00:29:05.400 --> 00:29:11.120
Then as they were getting ready to land, released the up input, pressed the A button correctly,

00:29:11.120 --> 00:29:16.100
but wait, in the middle of that, they also switched between the up input as they hit it

00:29:16.100 --> 00:29:20.740
in the air and then pressed the down input to go into the sit spin before releasing that

00:29:20.740 --> 00:29:25.520
one and pushing A to land the appropriate spin and then continue moving forward.

00:29:25.520 --> 00:29:26.560
Wow, what a nerd.

00:29:28.200 --> 00:29:33.940
And just, both of those, camel spin and sit spin are both pressed up or pressed down,

00:29:34.100 --> 00:29:37.500
but there are also diagonal presses, which I didn't even know that you could do on an

00:29:37.500 --> 00:29:41.080
NES controller. I was doing the diagonal presses and they all did the same move.

00:29:41.380 --> 00:29:43.920
Yeah, I think they end up doing like an up or a sideways move.

00:29:44.060 --> 00:29:46.200
It's very hard for it to register that you're hitting both.

00:29:46.260 --> 00:29:51.560
So it looks like the same move, but actually the up ones are doubles and the down ones are

00:29:51.560 --> 00:29:58.920
triples. So a down to the right is actually a triple axle jump, which I thought was like supposed

00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:04.400
to be the most impressive thing, but I guess a camel into sit spin would be more impressive.

00:30:04.600 --> 00:30:07.720
Yeah, the camel is so, it is impressive.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:09.680
Okay. I've never seen a camel.

00:30:09.940 --> 00:30:11.700
Yeah, so. It's just a camel.

00:30:11.860 --> 00:30:13.260
They just bring a camel out onto the ice.

00:30:13.460 --> 00:30:14.300
I've seen a camel.

00:30:14.780 --> 00:30:17.660
How was it? It peed a lot.

00:30:17.960 --> 00:30:20.020
Okay. Cool. Probably just like this game.

00:30:20.760 --> 00:30:22.320
Ha. This game wets the bed.

00:30:23.180 --> 00:30:26.240
All right. Anything else to say on figure skating?

00:30:27.280 --> 00:30:28.380
Nope. Great.

